close_reason: A timed-out managed npm update lookup reports npm_registry_lookup_timed_out and names its configurable budget; the Windows nightly freshness test no longer depends on a cold npm start
contract_change:
  api: "Managed npm update checks: update_error, update_check_reason, update_check_timeout_ms, ManagedExtensionRecord and PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS"
  before: "An npm update lookup that ran out of its fixed 10-second budget reported npm_registry_lookup_failed, like an unavailable registry, and ManagedExtensionRecord had no budget field"
  after: "It reports npm_registry_lookup_timed_out, and the managed record and extension summary carry update_check_timeout_ms naming the budget; other failures still report npm_registry_lookup_failed; PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS sets the budget (default 10000, clamped to 1000-120000)"
  migrate: "Match npm_registry_lookup_timed_out wherever npm_registry_lookup_failed is matched, add update_check_timeout_ms to any exhaustive keyof ManagedExtensionRecord mapping, and raise PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS for a slow registry or cold start"
escape_class: nightly_regression
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_strengthened
  owner: pm-5kfzjh
  gate_id: extension-update-check-deadline
  negative_control: "tests/unit/extensions/npm-update-check-timeout.spec.ts fails if a lookup that exits cleanly after its deadline is reported as its partial output, or if a failed tree teardown leaves the direct child running; tests/integration/extensions/update-check-process-tree.integration.spec.ts fails if the deadline waits for pipes held by a descendant (the round-1 AbortSignal runner waited for the full 30 s sleep)"
  local_checks[1]: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/extensions/npm-update-check-timeout.spec.ts tests/integration/extensions/update-check-process-tree.integration.spec.ts tests/integration/extensions/extension-diagnostic-purity.integration.spec.ts
  hosted_checks[2]: Gates (coverage),Windows regression (Node 24)
body: ""
